From 1a95bf3d423e47d0fac1a4d905b765561b6cddf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:59:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 62/91] moe-stream : copies of the GGUF parts on a second drive
 (SiegeLadder P16, LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_MIRROR=dir, off by default)

A cold prompt of 1K+ tokens touches most of the experts and is bounded by the drive (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.100: a
2.2K prompt reads 125 GB at 10.7 GB/s). With LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_MIRROR=dir, a part whose file of the same name and size
is found in dir, with the same bytes in 17 sampled 64 KiB blocks, gets a second llama_file (its own per-worker handle
pool). A worker reads a slab from the copy only while the primary drive already has LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_MIRROR_AT (8)
reads in flight and the copies fewer than LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_MIRROR_MAX (4): decode's shallow queue stays on the fast
drive, a prompt's overflow goes to the second one. Same bytes either way. print_stats reports the reads and bytes taken
from the copies. SiegeLadder runs.md 4.107: diskspd with the fork's reads, the PV593 (Gen5 x4) at 12 in flight 13.23
GB/s alone and 13.11 next to a VP4300 behind the chipset at 4 in flight (4.38) - 17.49 GB/s together.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
